    thinking: "**Initiating Server Setup**\n\nI\'m initiating the setup of the `server.ts` file now. My focus is on defining the system prompt for Gemini 1.5 Pro as per instructions. For the initial implementation, I\'m opting for an in-memory data store for issues and projects, and have just begun the import statements with express, path and multer, to handle server setup and file uploads.\n\n\n**Integrating AI and Server**\n\nI\'ve integrated the GoogleGenAI library and Vite server creation. I\'m focusing on setting up the server, including Multer for file uploads and an in-memory data store for issues and projects. Now I\'m initializing the Gemini AI with the API key and setting up data structures to store issues and projects. Finally, I\'m integrating the system instruction to define the role of the AI as a senior civic data architect and real-time multimodal analyst.\n\n\n**Defining AI Processing Parameters**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the AI\'s capabilities for processing citizen communications. I need to make sure the AI can handle diverse inputs like live audio, uploaded recordings, images, and location data. I\'m prioritizing accuracy in verifying legitimacy, extracting structural context from inputs, and translating regional accents and languages for precise JSON output. Filtering out irrelevant information is also essential.\n\n\n**Refining Communication Protocols**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the conversational protocol and output schema for the AI. Specifically, I\'m establishing how the AI will engage in live voice sessions and what follow-up questions it should ask. I\'m also ensuring the JSON output adheres precisely to the specified structure, including handling incomplete reports, and defining strict constraints. I\'m prioritizing direct JSON output without extra conversational elements, and the exact handling of \"is_legitimate_civic_issue\".\n\n\n**Implementing JSON Sanitization**\n\nI\'m now implementing JSON sanitization to handle potential model disobedience and ensure clean outputs. I\'m focusing on stripping markdown wrappers that the model sometimes adds, and then parsing the cleaned text. My main objective is to guarantee a reliable JSON structure. I\'m also preparing for priority calculations for new reports.\n\n\n**Finalizing Data Handling**\n\nI\'m now completing the implementation of the `/api/` endpoints to handle issues and projects. I\'ve integrated the processing of reports, including pushing new issues to the in-memory store. I\'ve also set up the GET endpoints to retrieve these issues and projects. Finally, I\'m setting up the server to run with Vite middleware in development or serve static files in production.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 30
      nanos: 965213755
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
