    thinking: "**Integrating Leaflet Map**\n\nI\'m in the process of replacing the placeholder `div` with a functional `react-leaflet` map. The initial component import includes `MapContainer`, `TileLayer`, `CircleMarker`, and `Popup` from the library. I need to make sure the leaflet CSS is properly included. Currently, I am testing the leaflet implementation.\n\n\n**Adding CSS**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the required Leaflet CSS to enable proper map rendering. Now, the map should render correctly with the `react-leaflet` components: `MapContainer`, `TileLayer`, `CircleMarker`, and `Popup`. I\'m using a CartoDB tile layer for a clean base map. The map is set to center around the coordinates [12.687, 78.615] and a zoom level of 13.\n\n\n**Implementing Map Markers**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data points, mapping each \"issue\" to a `CircleMarker` component.  I\'m using the `issues` array to populate the map. I\'ve configured the marker properties dynamically, including center coordinates, radius based on `priority_score`, and styling based on `priority_score` with different colors. Each marker now has a popup displaying detailed issue information from the data.\n\n\n"
