  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have completed the mobile optimization and added the missing core features you requested. Here is a summary of what has been implemented:\n\n- **Full Prototyping Login & Role Engine**: Upgraded the authentication screen to allow simple mocking of login roles (Citizen vs. Authority). As soon as you enter a name or email, you can toggle between the two roles directly on the login screen to simulate the respective interfaces.\n- **Location-Bound Intake**: In the citizen flow, the app immediately queries the user\'s location via geolocation APIs and binds it to the reporting component, enforcing accurate geospatial reporting instead of allowing random manual entries from anywhere.\n- **Geospatial Map & Active Ranking List**: The Citizen Dashboard now prominently features a dynamic map (powered by Leaflet) marking active civic issues nearby, alongside a verified upvote button.\n- **Dynamic Priority Recalculation**: When a citizen \"upvotes\" an issue on the map, the backend algorithm recalculates and immediately elevates its `priority_score` based on the combined severity and new vote count, pushing it up in the Authority\'s dashboard Execution Queue.\n- **Mobile Responsive Adjustments**: Engineered all data-heavy grid panels, map containers, and the voice reporter components with proper flex columns and bounding boxes (`h-auto` to fixed `lg:h` sizes) to ensure they stack perfectly and take up appropriate viewport sizes on narrow mobile screens."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
