  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully integrated the multi-language support, fixed the map rendering, and refactored the layout into a Reddit-like civic feed.\n\n- **Reddit-style Civic Feed**: Re-architected the `CitizenDashboard` into a multi-column layout. The central column now acts as a **Live Feed**, displaying both reported civic issues and ongoing municipal projects. I implemented robust upvoting logic for both issues and projects, mimicking a social feed to prioritize high-visibility community concerns.\n- **Multilingual Support**: Extracted the UI strings into an internationalization framework (`i18n.ts`) supporting **English, Hindi, Tamil, Kannada, and Telugu**. The active language dynamically translates both the UI elements on the dashboard and the live voice assistant.\n- **Context-Aware Voice Assistant**: Passed the user\'s language selection directly to the backend WebSocket stream. The AI agent\'s system instructions are now overridden on the fly, instructing the live assistant to converse exclusively in the user\'s chosen local language.\n- **Map Visibility Fixes**: Refactored the `react-leaflet` CSS imports and implemented absolute height constraints on the `MapContainer` so that the map renders reliably on all devices. Additionally, I added a default geographical coordinate fallback so that the map will still load even if the browser (or preview environment) delays or denies geolocation access."
