  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying System Status**\n\nThe development server restart was successful, and I\'ve conducted a final systems check. The missing map issue was resolved. A `location` value was being set to null due to potential sandbox environment geolocation issues. To solve this, I initialized the location directly with local coordinates.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed a deep-dive review and implemented solutions for the reporting (add) and login flows, fixing the map visibility, and bringing a fully functional \"Reddit-for-local-governance\" experience to life.\n\n### \360\237\214\237 Summary of Key Enhancements\n\n#### 1. Added \"Quick Post\" (Deterministic Manual Submission)\n*   **Intuitive Toggle**: Added a third tab (**Quick Post**) in `VoiceReporter.tsx` alongside **AI Form** and **AI Live** to allow direct, immediate posts exactly like Reddit.\n*   **Rich Form Input**: Built a form to select a category (e.g., *Roads*, *Water Supply*, *Sanitation*, *Electricity*, *Public Safety*), write a detailed description, select an explicit severity rating (1\342\200\2235), and post.\n*   **Direct REST API Endpoint**: Added a new `/api/issues` `POST` endpoint to `server.ts` that immediately processes, prioritizes, and inserts the manual issue at local coordinates.\n*   **GPS Fallback Location**: Enhanced coordinates parsing so that if GPS is blocked by browser/iframe sandboxes, newly posted issues automatically get randomized offsets centered on the active ward, ensuring they appear instantly on the map!\n\n#### 2. Resolved Map Visibility Bug (\"Locating you...\")\n*   **Instant Rendering**: Changed `CitizenDashboard.tsx` to initialize `location` with the local ward center (`[12.687, 78.615]`) and removed the blocking null-check conditional. The Leaflet map now renders instantly on mount!\n*   **Non-Blocking Geolocation**: Configured browser geolocation with a rapid timeout fallback (`4000` ms) so it won\'t hang the UI in restricted sandbox environments.\n\n#### 3. Polished Sign-In & On-the-Fly Translation\n*   **Login Language Selector**: Fixed the Sign-In screen which was previously hardcoding language to `\'en\'`, and added a preferred language select dropdown directly to the login form.\n*   **Interactive Navbar Language Switcher**: Added a beautiful language dropdown (`Globe` icon) in the header Navbar, enabling logged-in citizens to switch the entire application interface (English, Hindi, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada) dynamically on the fly!\n\n#### 4. Project Sentiment & Downvoting\n*   **Dual-Option Voting**: Added a **Thumbs Down / Object** button next to Thumbs Up in the citizen project feed. This dynamically connects with the backend `/api/projects/:id/vote` to register criticisms, updating the AI sentiment monitor in real time.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 106090361
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
