    thinking: "**Defining the Architecture**\n\nI\'ve digested the `gemini-api` skill. Now, I\'m delineating the implementation and modification aspects. The plan is crystallized; I\'m moving toward an elegant design. Focusing now on a photo upload thing, specifically how it integrates into the \"Quick Post\" functionality. I\'m considering the user flow in detail.\n\n\n**Refining the Endpoint**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `app.post(\'/api/issues\')` endpoint modification. I\'m exploring multipart form requests to handle image uploads alongside text, category, and other data. I\'ve integrated a Gemini API call using `gemini-3.5-flash` with the system instruction to assess the image and text submitted in a quick post. I am now working on error handling within the API.\n\n\n**Implementing the Verification Endpoint**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new backend endpoint `/api/issues/:id/photo`. This endpoint will handle image uploads and integrate with Gemini for analysis. I\'m focusing on handling multipart form requests and using Gemini to verify the image\'s legitimacy as a civic issue. I will update the issue\'s metadata (category, summary, etc.) based on Gemini\'s assessment, and I\'ll save the image as base64 in memory. I will also incorporate visual verification flags in the UI. I have also moved on to fixing the multiple upvoting problem, by using local storage.\n\n\n**Improving the UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI refinements, specifically the aesthetic. I\'ll be working to improve the visual design across several components: `CitizenDashboard.tsx`, `Dashboard.tsx`, and `VoiceReporter.tsx`. My goal is to achieve a professional, premium look. I\'m moving toward a minimalist cream/charcoal/sandalwood theme. I\'ll clean up the typography and spacing. I\'ll also add high-contrast fonts, consistent padding, and elegant visual badges.\n\n\n**Enhancing the Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI improvements, specifically layout. I\'m focusing on defining clear boundaries and avoiding unnecessary clutter, like complex sidebars. The map needs beautiful containerization and responsiveness, and I\'ll include uploaded photos on issue cards. The project doesn\'t require extra package installation. I verified the server starts correctly, and now I\'m inspecting how the backend manages issues in `server.ts`. I also devised a plan to store base64-encoded image data directly within issue objects, which is a robust strategy.\n\n\n**Modifying the POST Endpoint**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the `/api/issues` POST endpoint and how image uploads will be handled. I plan to use `multer` to accept `multipart/form-data`, specifically using `upload.single(\'image\')`. Gemini will assess the images for legitimacy. If the image is legitimate, I\'ll set its status to OPEN and `is_verified` to true and store the image. If the image is spam, I\'ll mark it as SPAM, ensuring a clear \"SPAM/FAKE REJECTED\" banner is shown to provide a clear user feedback.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view `server.ts` from lines 230 to 290 to examine the exact signature of the `/api/issues` endpoints."
