  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adjusting Issue Endpoints**\n\nI\'m currently reworking the `/api/issues` endpoint. My focus is on ensuring it can handle both JSON payloads for quick posts and multipart payloads that include image uploads and additional details like `category` and `executive_summary`. I\'m aiming for flexible and robust input processing.\n\n\n**Refining Input Processing**\n\nI\'ve hit on a really elegant solution! Using `multer` with `upload.single(\'image\')` lets `/api/issues` gracefully handle both JSON and multipart form data. If `req.file` is undefined, it\'s a standard JSON post, and the body parses as usual. But with multipart, `multer` also populates `req.body`! Now, when an image is uploaded, I\'m integrating Gemini. I\'ll extract base64 data and call `gemini-3.5-flash` with a targeted prompt to verify the image\'s legitimacy and identify civic issues.\n\n\n**Integrating Gemini Output**\n\nI\'ve got Gemini\'s response structure nailed down. I am able to parse the JSON output from `gemini-3.5-flash`. I\'m going to set up automated handling: If Gemini flags something as spam, the issue status updates to \'REJECTED\' (or similar). If legitimate, it becomes \'OPEN,\' `is_verified` is set to `true`, and I adjust the `severity_score` and `category` according to Gemini\'s analysis. The `visual_analysis_summary` provides rich details.\n\n\n**Expanding Image Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/issues/:id/photo` endpoint to allow photo updates for existing issues. I\'ll re-run Gemini analysis for verification, pulling the `executive_summary` for context. This involves updating `image_url` with the base64 image data and storing the `visual_analysis` string. Verification success updates `is_verified` and potentially `severity_score`/`category`, while spam flags will update issue status to \'REJECTED\'. I\'ve verified `issues` is properly defined.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will edit `server.ts` to enhance the `/api/issues` POST endpoint to support image uploads, process the image via the Gemini API to verify if it\'s legitimate or spam, and create a new POST endpoint `/api/issues/:id/photo` to handle post-live-call photo attachments."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 643672941
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
