  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Trigger**\n\nI\'m now tracing the \"Report Logged\" trigger back through `LiveOperator.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining how the `report_submitted` event leads to the `setReportSubmitted` function, and the subsequent `stopLiveSession` call. This is making the connection between the \"report submitted\" event and how a live session is brought to an end.\n\n\n**Connecting the Report**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `report_submitted` event, specifically within `server.ts`. I\'m verifying the inclusion of the `newIssue` ID in the WebSocket message. This is crucial as I need to capture it after a call or report submission. I plan to use that `issue` ID to trigger a \"add visual evidence\" pop-up. I\'m now going to explore what to do with the `newIssue` in `LiveOperator.tsx`.\n\n\n**Refining the Flow**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s feedback, which really clarifies the flow! I\'m planning to modify `LiveOperator` to pass the submitted issue to `VoiceReporter`. I plan to render `LiveOperator` in `VoiceReporter` using an `onLiveReportSubmitted` prop that takes the issue. I\'ll use state in `VoiceReporter` to set a `liveReportIssue`, then render a polished overlay popup when that state updates. I love the idea of the \"\360\237\223\270 Add Visual Evidence to Live\" prompt!\n\n\n**Implementing Image Uploads**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating image uploads for both report verification and quick posts. For the report verification, I\'ll add a file picker with drag-and-drop functionality, uploading images to `/api/issues/${liveReportIssue.issue_id}/photo` as `FormData`. This upload triggers Gemini analysis with a loading state, and then a \"Verified!\" success message. For quick posts within `VoiceReporter.tsx`, I\'ll include a styled \"Add Photo\" button/drag-and-drop zone with a preview. Both submissions send a `FormData` object with the image, if present, to the `/api/issues` endpoint.\n\n\n**Refactoring the Function**\n\nI\'m now refactoring `LiveOperator.tsx` to support the `onLiveReportSubmitted` prop. I\'ve updated the component\'s type definition and added a conditional call within the `wsRef.current.onmessage` handler for the `report_submitted` event. The conditional checks for the presence of the prop and `submittedIssue` and then calls the prop, passing in the issue. I\'ve also reconsidered the timing of `stopLiveSession` so that the pop-up can remain.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will edit `LiveOperator.tsx` to add support for the `onLiveReportSubmitted` prop, so the parent component can know when a report has been logged and capture its issue details for the follow-up photo upload."
