  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Tracking User Votes**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about the backend implementation for user upvotes on issues. The plan is to store the `userId` in the `issue.upvoted_by` array whenever a user upvotes. I\'ll need to make sure to initialize the array if it doesn\'t already exist. I will be checking `/api/issues` next.\n\n\n**Implementing Upvote Endpoint**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/issues/:id/upvote` endpoint. I\'ve considered that the endpoint should toggle upvotes, allowing users to remove their votes. I\'ve also implemented a `citizen_upvote_count` field, and I\'m currently recalculating the priority score after each upvote/downvote action. I will need to verify the implementation to ensure it works correctly with the `userId` in either the request body or the headers, allowing for anonymous users.\n\n\n**Refining Priority Formula**\n\nI\'ve refined the priority calculation using 2.0 * Sg + 1.5 * Math.log(Vc + 1) + 1.0 * (deltaT / 24). Also, I\'m updating `issue.updated_at` and returning the `has_upvoted` status. The implementation supports a unique `userId` from the request body or header. I\'m now thinking about project votes next.\n\n\n**Analyzing Project Votes**\n\nI\'m now diving into project vote logic, considering cases where users toggle off, switch votes, or cast fresh votes. I\'m incrementing/decrementing positive votes and negative criticisms accordingly within the `sentiment_summary`. The `voted_users` object stores the userId and the vote state. This also accounts for vote deletion, ensuring that counts never go below zero.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view lines 100 to 250 of `CitizenDashboard.tsx` to see how the frontend sends upvote and vote requests to the backend."
