  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Summarizing Progress on Tasks**\n\nI\'m making excellent progress on crafting the final summary. I\'ve successfully reviewed the project\'s key requests and the completed accomplishments. Specifically, I\'ve noted the implementation of photo uploads, with an optional photo attachment feature now available in Quick.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have implemented all the requested features and visual refinements to resolve the outstanding issues. Here is a design and functional overview of the updates:\n\n### 1. Photo Upload & Visual Evidence\n*   **Quick Post Photo Option**: Added a styled photo-upload zone directly within the **Quick Post (Manual)** form. Citizens can capture or attach an image to accompany their reports.\n*   **Post-Live Call Overlay**: Created a follow-up modal that appears automatically once an **AI Live Session** concludes. It prompts the user to add accompanying photo evidence to the newly created report.\n\n### 2. Intelligent Backend Verification (Gemini API)\n*   **Multimodal Spam Guardrails**: Implemented server-side image validation using `gemini-3.5-flash`. When an image is uploaded, Gemini analyzes the image alongside the user\'s description:\n    *   **Legitimacy Check**: Verifies if the image shows an actual municipal issue (e.g., potholes, sanitation failures, streetlights). Unrelated graphics, selfies, or memes are flagged as **Spam** and labeled in red with Gemini\'s detailed explanation.\n    *   **Audit Extractions**: Automatically corrects categories, refines severity ratings (1\342\200\2235), and saves a machine-readable `visual_analysis` text summary displayed on the card.\n\n### 3. Restricting Multiple Votes (Reddit-Style)\n*   **Persistent Citizen Identity**: Added unique local citizen IDs (`cit_######`) generated and stored in the browser\'s `localStorage`.\n*   **Idempotent & Toggle Voting**: Upgraded `/api/issues/:id/upvote` and `/api/projects/:id/vote` endpoints to keep track of voting user IDs. A user can now vote exactly once; clicking a vote a second time toggles it off, and switching project sentiment works seamlessly.\n\n### 4. UI Polish & Visual Rhythm\n*   **Status Badges**: Added high-contrast status tags showing **\342\234\223 AI Verified** or **\342\235\214 Spam Filtered**.\n*   **Visual Enhancements**: Feed cards now feature structured metadata, robotic diagnostic sub-notes summarizing Gemini\'s visual audits, custom-styled error banners for rejected items, and high-contrast image thumbnails."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 966674961
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
